Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: ppe: propagate SRAM flush errors

The loop-local err shadows the value returned by the initialization helper.
A failed SRAM commit stops the loop but the caller still receives success
and continues initializing PPE with an incompletely cleared table.

Use the existing outer err so the first commit error reaches the existing
PPE and Ethernet probe error paths. Successful and empty flushes still
return zero, and no later entry is touched after an error.

---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -1445,8 +1445,6 @@
 	int i, err = 0;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < sram_num_entries; i++) {
-		int err;
-
 		memset(&hwe[i], 0, sizeof(*hwe));
 		err = airoha_ppe_foe_commit_sram_entry(ppe, i);
 		if (err)
